WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.440
What would a house payment leave you

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:04.320
each month? Start there, before deciding what

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.880
payment feels comfortable. Check whether the quote

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:10.660
includes taxes, insurance and any association dues.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:12.880
A quoted amount may leave some costs

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:16.240
separate. Then allow for utilities, maintenance and

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:18.560
the other bills you already pay, along

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:19.840
with the savings you want to keep

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:22.760
making. Count each expense once.

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:24.440
If an amount is missing, keep it

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.640
as a question rather than guessing.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.760
That's the conversation the payment workbook helps

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:31.600
you prepare. Review your answers before sending

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.000
them to me, or print the page

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.010
for yourself.
